   int64_t restartAfter = 1200000;
 
   // Room scanning
+  /// How many rooms `scanBest` examines per slot when a class's room domain is larger than
+  /// `roomScanFullBelow`, and the threshold itself.
+  ///
+  /// These were inherited from the TypeScript solver's tuning, where a faculty had a few dozen
+  /// rooms. They bind hard on a class that names **no** room at all: its domain is every room the
+  /// faculty owns — 582 on a n = 12 288 university — so the scan sees 16 % of its options, and the
+  /// campaign's instance characterisation found that instances with more such classes are markedly
+  /// worse (CAMPAIGN-LOG.md §6k). Raising them costs throughput per candidate; whether the trade
+  /// pays is measured rather than assumed.
   int roomSample = 96;
   int roomScanFullBelow = 256;
 
+  /// How many rooms per slot `scanBest` prices for travel before it stops paying for the exact
+  /// O(bucket) journey check and scores the rest as though the journey were free.
+  ///
+  /// Six was fine while a room domain meant "a handful of rooms in one корпус", where the omitted
+  /// rooms were in that корпус too and the omission was worth nothing. It is not fine on a class
+  /// that names no room: the domain is every room the faculty owns, spread over every корпус, so 90
+  /// of the 96 sampled rooms are scored travel-free and the operator proposes journeys the
+  /// acceptance test then rejects. Exposed so that "the budget is the problem" can be separated from
+  /// "the sample is the problem" — see `roomBuildingFirst`, which fixes the same thing without
+  /// paying for it.
+  int roomTravelBudget = 6;
+
+  /// Scan the rooms that need no journey first, when it can be proved cheaply that they need none.
+  ///
+  /// `State::buildingsOn` gives, in one pass per slot, the set of buildings this class's own
+  /// lecturers and groups already occupy that day. When that set is a **single** building, every
+  /// room in it has `journeyMinutes == 0` against every one of those classes, so such a room is
+  /// travel-free by construction — no per-room travel evaluation needed, and no travel violation
+  /// possible from this placement. The scan therefore spends its whole `roomSample` budget on those
+  /// rooms and only falls through to the rest if they yielded nothing usable.
+  ///
+  /// Deliberately narrow. With two or more buildings already in use, "same building as something"
+  /// no longer implies "no journey", and the filter is not applied at all rather than applied on a
+  /// premise that does not hold. Off by default until measured.
+  bool roomBuildingFirst = false;
+
+  /// Answer "is this room free?" from the room bucket's occupancy mask instead of walking the
+  /// room's day. 0 off, 1 fast path, 2 fast path and no walk at all.
+  ///
+  /// Level 1 is **behaviour-identical**: `State::roomFreeAt` agrees with `roomClashesAt(...) == 0`
